Main code compiles. Now write tests. Test resources application.yaml (separate named DB), MutableClock, BaseIntegrationTest, then test classes.

Test application.yaml:
```yaml
spring:
  datasource:
    url: jdbc:h2:mem:snowpack-test;MODE=MySQL;DB_CLOSE_DELAY=-1
    username: sa
    password:
    driver-class-name: org.h2.Driver
```

BaseIntegrationTest: @SpringBootTest + @AutoConfigureMockMvc, nested @TestConfiguration providing MutableClock @Primary. Cleanup in @BeforeEach: DELETE FROM tables. Helper methods to post readings via service or mockMvc.

MutableClock:
```java
public class MutableClock extends Clock {
    private Instant instant;
    private ZoneId zone;
    public MutableClock(Instant instant, ZoneId zone) {...}
    getZone, withZone, instant, setInstant, plus
}
```

Tests:

ReadingApiTest (MockMvc):
1. postReadingSuccessAndReplay: POST reading → 200, overLimit false; replay same body → 200 same id, replayed true; same requestId different newSnowCm → 409 REQUEST_ID_CONFLICT.
2. nonHourlyRejected: hourUtc with minutes → 422 NON_HOURLY_TIMESTAMP.
3. duplicateHourRejected: post hour H, then different requestId same hour → 409 DUPLICATE_HOUR_READING.
4. overLimitReadingCreatesClosureAndInvalidates: close zone first? Scenario: zone open; post 3 good readings; manual closure; first review confirm (alice) via service or API; then post over-limit reading → response closureCreated false (already closed), reviewsInvalidated 1; status shows review INVALIDATED with reason. Also new zone: over-limit reading on open zone → closureCreated true, status CLOSED.
5. errataAppended: post reading, post errata → 200; replay errata → replayed true; errata with same requestId different note → 409; errata for missing reading → 404.
6. manualClosureReplayAndConflict: post closure → 200; again same → replayed; again different reason same requestId → 409; closure when closed → 409 ZONE_ALREADY_CLOSED.

ReleaseReviewApiTest (MockMvc):
1. happyPath: manual closure, 3 readings (4,5,5), alice confirm → IN_PROGRESS; bob confirm → COMPLETED decisionVersion 1; status OPEN; timeline has CLOSURE and RELEASE; closure lifted. Then new over-limit reading → new closure created, decision retained: status CLOSED, timeline still has RELEASE v1 plus new CLOSURE.
2. synthetic 4,5,6 rejected: closure, readings 4,5,6 → alice confirm → 422 OVER_LIMIT_READING_IN_WINDOW.
3. missingHour: closure, readings at 08:00 and 10:00 (gap) → 422 MISSING_HOURLY_READING. Also fewer than 3 → 422.
4. sameReviewer: closure, 3 good readings, alice, alice → 422 SAME_REVIEWER.
5. zoneNotClosed: readings only, confirm → 409 ZONE_NOT_CLOSED.
6. overLimitInvalidatesPendingReview: closure, 3 good readings, alice confirm; post over-limit reading (new hour) → reviewsInvalidated 1; bob confirm → 409? Let's trace: review invalidated; bob confirm with new requestId → no in-progress → startReview path → zone CLOSED → window: latest 3 include over-limit reading → 422 OVER_LIMIT_READING_IN_WINDOW. So expect 422. And status latestReview INVALIDATED with reason OVER_LIMIT_READING.
7. staleVersion: closure, 3 good readings, alice confirm; post within-limit reading (new hour, newSnow 2) → bob confirm → 409 STALE_READING_VERSION.
8. reviewReplay: alice confirm with requestId v1; replay v1 same reviewer → replayed true; v1 with different reviewer → 409.

ConcurrencyTest (service-level, real H2):
1. concurrentSecondConfirmSingleVersion: setup zone closed, 3 readings, alice first confirm (via service). Two threads confirm bob/carol with latch. Assert: exactly one success with decisionVersion 1, other throws BusinessException 409 (ZONE_NOT_CLOSED? let's trace: loser sees review COMPLETED, no in-progress → startReview → zone now OPEN → 409 ZONE_NOT_CLOSED). Assert release_decision count == 1 for zone. Assert zone OPEN.
2. confirmVsOverLimitReadingRace: setup same, alice confirmed. Thread A: bob confirm; thread B: post over-limit reading at next hour. Run concurrently, collect outcomes. Assert invariants: decisions ≤ 1; if decision exists → closures count == 2 and zone CLOSED and review COMPLETED; else review INVALIDATED and zone CLOSED and closures == 1. Also final status consistent.

For counting rows use JdbcTemplate directly.

Note: service confirm is @Transactional; calling from multiple threads via Spring bean works.

For the race test, outcomes depend on timing; assertions must cover both. Use CountDownLatch to start simultaneously.

Timeouts: use Future.get(15, SECONDS).

MutableClock usage: set fixed instant per test; assert createdAt? Maybe assert reading createdAt equals clock instant in one test （时间测试用可控时钟）. I'll assert in reading test that response... ReadingResult doesn't include createdAt. Status timeline CLOSURE at = clock time. In manual closure test, set clock to fixed instant, then GET status and assert timeline CLOSURE at equals that instant. Good.

BaseIntegrationTest:

```java
@SpringBootTest
@AutoConfigureMockMvc
public abstract class BaseIntegrationTest {
    @Autowired protected MockMvc mockMvc;
    @Autowired protected JdbcTemplate jdbc;
    @Autowired protected MutableClock clock;

    @TestConfiguration
    static class ClockConfig {
        @Bean @Primary
        MutableClock mutableClock() { return new MutableClock(Instant.parse("2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"), ZoneOffset.UTC); }
    }

    @BeforeEach
    void cleanDatabase() {
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM release_decision");
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM release_review");
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM reading_errata");
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM snow_reading");
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM closure_command");
        jdbc.update("DELETE FROM zone_state");
        clock.setInstant(Instant.parse("2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"));
    }
